Evaluating the same prescribed low-intensity woodland burns, forester Jian Zhou observes that autumn burns better protect nesting canopy birds while still clearing dry fuel. Consequently, forester Jian Zhou cautions against adopting the practice without targeted safeguards.$hdsat_report_fix$, prompt = $hdsat_report_fix$Based on the texts, on what point do ecologist Mara Vance and forester Jian Zhou most clearly differ regarding prescribed low-intensity woodland burns?$hdsat_report_fix$, choices = $hdsat_report_fix$[{"id":"A","text":"ecologist Mara Vance opposes prescribed low-intensity woodland burns on financial grounds, whereas forester Jian Zhou supports it unconditionally."},{"id":"B","text":"ecologist Mara Vance studies only laboratory models, whereas forester Jian Zhou refuses to consider empirical data."},{"id":"C","text":"Ecologist Mara Vance stresses prescribed low-intensity woodland burns's main benefit; forester Jian Zhou notes an operational trade-off."},{"id":"D","text":"Both authors conclude that prescribed low-intensity woodland burns is obsolete compared with nineteenth-century methods."}]$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, figure_metadata = NULL, skill = $hdsat_report_fix$Cross-Text Connections$hdsat_report_fix$, domain = $hdsat_report_fix$Craft and Structure$hdsat_report_fix$, difficulty = $hdsat_report_fix$Hard$hdsat_report_fix$, format = $hdsat_report_fix$multiple_choice$hdsat_report_fix$, assessments = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$SAT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT/NMSQT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 10$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 8/9$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-CRF-88402$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.question_keys SET correct_answer = $hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$, acceptable_answers = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], explanation = $hdsat_report_fix$Text 1 highlights how spring burns maximize understory wildflower diversity, whereas Text 2 notes that autumn burns better protect nesting canopy birds while still clearing dry fuel. 'ecologist Mara Vance emphasizes the primary performance advantage of prescribed low-intensity woodland burns, whereas forester Jian Zhou focuses on a secondary operational trade-off.' accurately synthesizes how the two perspectives relate.$hdsat_report_fix$, distractor_rationales = $hdsat_report_fix${"A":"“ecologist Mara Vance opposes prescribed low-intensity woodland burns on financial grounds, whereas forester Jian Zhou supports it unconditionally.” overstates or misstates the disagreement between the two authors.","D":"“Both authors conclude that prescribed low-intensity woodland burns is obsolete compared with nineteenth-century methods.” overstates or misstates the disagreement between the two authors.","B":"“ecologist Mara Vance studies only laboratory models, whereas forester Jian Zhou refuses to consider empirical data.” overstates or misstates the disagreement between the two authors."}$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, updated_at = NOW() WHERE question_id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-CRF-88402$hdsat_report_fix$;
