UPDATE public.questions SET stimulus = $hdsat_report_fix$While researching bioluminescent dinoflagellate defense mechanisms (study note set 3), a student has taken the following notes:
• Lingulodinium polyedra is a marine dinoflagellate species that emits brief blue light flashes when mechanically agitated.
• Laboratory shear-flow experiments show that a single cell flash lasts approximately 100 milliseconds at 475 nanometers wavelength.
• When grazing copepods disturb the water, the resulting flashes startle the copepods and reduce their feeding rates by 55%.
• The flashes also illuminate the copepods, making them visible to nocturnal predatory fish from up to two meters away.
• Cultures kept under constant light lose their circadian bioluminescence rhythm within four days.$hdsat_report_fix$, prompt = $hdsat_report_fix$The student wants to explain how bioluminescence protects Lingulodinium polyedra in two distinct ways. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$hdsat_report_fix$, choices = $hdsat_report_fix$[{"id":"A","text":"Nocturnal predatory fish can spot illuminated prey from distances of up to two meters in dark water."},{"id":"B","text":"Laboratory cultures of Lingulodinium polyedra lose their circadian rhythm if kept under constant illumination for four days."},{"id":"C","text":"Its blue flashes startle grazing copepods and expose them to nocturnal predatory fish."},{"id":"D","text":"Lingulodinium polyedra emits 100-millisecond flashes at a wavelength of 475 nanometers when mechanically agitated."}]$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, figure_metadata = NULL, skill = $hdsat_report_fix$Rhetorical Synthesis$hdsat_report_fix$, domain = $hdsat_report_fix$Expression of Ideas$hdsat_report_fix$, difficulty = $hdsat_report_fix$Hard$hdsat_report_fix$, format = $hdsat_report_fix$multiple_choice$hdsat_report_fix$, assessments = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$SAT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT/NMSQT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 10$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 8/9$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-EXP-89022$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.question_keys SET correct_answer = $hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$, acceptable_answers = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], explanation = $hdsat_report_fix$The notes describe two distinct defenses: the flash startles grazing copepods and cuts their feeding by 55%, and it makes the copepods visible to nocturnal predatory fish. The choice that names both mechanisms is correct; the others mention only one effect or an unrelated detail.$hdsat_report_fix$, distractor_rationales = $hdsat_report_fix${"D":"“Lingulodinium polyedra emits 100-millisecond flashes at a wavelength of 475 nanometers when mechanically agitated.” does not accomplish the stated goal: it either leaves out a required detail or emphasizes a tangential note.","B":"“Laboratory cultures of Lingulodinium polyedra lose their circadian rhythm if kept under constant illumination for four days.” does not accomplish the stated goal: it either leaves out a required detail or emphasizes a tangential note.","A":"“Nocturnal predatory fish can spot illuminated prey from distances of up to two meters in dark water.” does not accomplish the stated goal: it either leaves out a required detail or emphasizes a tangential note."}$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, updated_at = NOW() WHERE question_id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-EXP-89022$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.questions SET stimulus = $hdsat_report_fix$Copper printing plates wear down after roughly two thousand impressions—a feature documented across three seasons—____$hdsat_report_fix$, prompt = $hdsat_report_fix$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to Standard English?$hdsat_report_fix$, choices = $hdsat_report_fix$[{"id":"A","text":"; so editions of ten thousand prints require the plates to be recut several times."},{"id":"B","text":"editions of ten thousand prints require the plates to be recut several times."},{"id":"C","text":"so editions of ten thousand prints require the plates to be recut several times."},{"id":"D","text":"and, editions of ten thousand prints require the plates to be recut several times."}]$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, figure_metadata = NULL, skill = $hdsat_report_fix$Boundaries$hdsat_report_fix$, domain = $hdsat_report_fix$Standard English Conventions$hdsat_report_fix$, difficulty = $hdsat_report_fix$Easy$hdsat_report_fix$, format = $hdsat_report_fix$multiple_choice$hdsat_report_fix$, assessments = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$SAT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT/NMSQT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 10$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 8/9$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-SEC-89358$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.question_keys SET correct_answer = $hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$, acceptable_answers = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], explanation = $hdsat_report_fix$The second em dash closes the parenthetical phrase. 'So' introduces the result: because a plate wears out after roughly two thousand impressions, a ten-thousand-print edition requires the plates to be recut several times.$hdsat_report_fix$, distractor_rationales = $hdsat_report_fix${"A":"A semicolon followed by 'so' is not a standard way to join these clauses.","B":"Without a conjunction or punctuation, the two clauses form a run-on.","D":"The comma after 'and' is incorrectly placed and does not fix the boundary."}$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, updated_at = NOW() WHERE question_id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-SEC-89358$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.questions SET stimulus = $hdsat_report_fix$The field station lost power for six hours ______ a failed breaker, a flooded generator, and a downed line.$hdsat_report_fix$, prompt = $hdsat_report_fix$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$hdsat_report_fix$, choices = $hdsat_report_fix$[{"id":"A","text":";"},{"id":"B","text":","},{"id":"C","text":":"},{"id":"D","text":"."}]$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, figure_metadata = NULL, skill = $hdsat_report_fix$Boundaries$hdsat_report_fix$, domain = $hdsat_report_fix$Standard English Conventions$hdsat_report_fix$, difficulty = $hdsat_report_fix$Easy$hdsat_report_fix$, format = $hdsat_report_fix$multiple_choice$hdsat_report_fix$, assessments = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$SAT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT/NMSQT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 10$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 8/9$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-SEC-9003$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.question_keys SET correct_answer = $hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$, acceptable_answers = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], explanation = $hdsat_report_fix$A colon introduces the list that identifies the three causes. A semicolon must join two independent clauses, a comma cannot introduce this list, and a period would require a new sentence beginning with a capital letter.$hdsat_report_fix$, distractor_rationales = $hdsat_report_fix${"A":"A semicolon must join two independent clauses; the list is not an independent clause.","B":"A comma cannot introduce this list; it would splice the sentence together.","D":"A period would end the sentence, so the list would need to begin a new capitalised sentence."}$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, updated_at = NOW() WHERE question_id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-SEC-9003$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.questions SET stimulus = $hdsat_report_fix$The plan rested on three assumptions ______ demand would stay flat, shipping costs would remain stable, and no competitor would enter the market.$hdsat_report_fix$, prompt = $hdsat_report_fix$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$hdsat_report_fix$, choices = $hdsat_report_fix$[{"id":"A","text":";"},{"id":"B","text":","},{"id":"C","text":":"},{"id":"D","text":"."}]$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, figure_metadata = NULL, skill = $hdsat_report_fix$Boundaries$hdsat_report_fix$, domain = $hdsat_report_fix$Standard English Conventions$hdsat_report_fix$, difficulty = $hdsat_report_fix$Easy$hdsat_report_fix$, format = $hdsat_report_fix$multiple_choice$hdsat_report_fix$, assessments = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$SAT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT/NMSQT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 10$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 8/9$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-SEC-9033$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.question_keys SET correct_answer = $hdsat_report_fix$C$hdsat_report_fix$, acceptable_answers = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$B$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], explanation = $hdsat_report_fix$A colon introduces the list that spells out the three assumptions. The semicolon does not join independent clauses here, the comma splices, and the period would leave a lower-case sentence after it.$hdsat_report_fix$, distractor_rationales = $hdsat_report_fix${"A":"A semicolon must join independent clauses; the list is not an independent clause.","B":"A comma cannot introduce this list without creating a splice.","D":"A period would require a new sentence with a capital letter."}$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, updated_at = NOW() WHERE question_id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-SEC-9033$hdsat_report_fix$;
UPDATE public.questions SET stimulus = $hdsat_report_fix$Text 1
The novelist argued that writing by hand slows composition enough to improve sentence rhythm, because the pace forces writers to rehearse each phrase before committing it.

Text 2
The writing researcher agreed that pace affects rhythm but noted that dictation can produce comparable rehearsal, since speakers must plan whole clauses before voicing them.$hdsat_report_fix$, prompt = $hdsat_report_fix$Which choice best describes the relationship between the two texts?$hdsat_report_fix$, choices = $hdsat_report_fix$[{"id":"A","text":"Text 1 rejects the idea that rhythm matters, while Text 2 defends it."},{"id":"B","text":"Both texts claim that typing is the best way to compose."},{"id":"C","text":"Text 2 argues that planning has no effect on rhythm."},{"id":"D","text":"Both texts value planning before committing words, though they name different tools for it."}]$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, figure_metadata = NULL, skill = $hdsat_report_fix$Cross-Text Connections$hdsat_report_fix$, domain = $hdsat_report_fix$Craft and Structure$hdsat_report_fix$, difficulty = $hdsat_report_fix$Hard$hdsat_report_fix$, format = $hdsat_report_fix$multiple_choice$hdsat_report_fix$, assessments = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$SAT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT/NMSQT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 10$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 8/9$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-CRF-90800-2$hdsat_report_fix$;
