UPDATE public.questions SET stimulus = $hdsat_report_fix$Antarctic sponges grow extremely slowly, adding only a fraction of a millimetre each year. A specimen collected at 200 meters had growth bands that took decades to form. Because the bands record the chemistry of the water in which they formed, a single large sponge can preserve a record of changing ocean conditions stretching back further than most instrument series.

______$hdsat_report_fix$, prompt = $hdsat_report_fix$Which choice most logically completes the text?$hdsat_report_fix$, choices = $hdsat_report_fix$[{"id":"A","text":"Growth bands are unrelated to the chemistry of the surrounding water."},{"id":"B","text":"Instrument series are always longer than a sponge's growth record."},{"id":"C","text":"Antarctic sponges grow quickly enough to record daily changes in seawater."},{"id":"D","text":"Old sponges can serve as archives of ocean chemistry."}]$hdsat_report_fix$::jsonb, figure_metadata = NULL, skill = $hdsat_report_fix$Inferences$hdsat_report_fix$, domain = $hdsat_report_fix$Information and Ideas$hdsat_report_fix$, difficulty = $hdsat_report_fix$Hard$hdsat_report_fix$, format = $hdsat_report_fix$multiple_choice$hdsat_report_fix$, assessments = ARRAY[$hdsat_report_fix$SAT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT/NMSQT$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 10$hdsat_report_fix$, $hdsat_report_fix$PSAT 8/9$hdsat_report_fix$]::TEXT[], updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $hdsat_report_fix$RW-M10P-0151$hdsat_report_fix$;
